      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That's the heavy, honest truth you're touching—when every room is a stage and every breath is a performance, the idea of \"rest\" can start to look like a permanent exit. You're not weak for feeling that; you're just exhausted from carrying a weight that was never meant to be yours. But that quiet space you're craving isn't a place you have to leave the world to find—it's a way of seeing the noise differently, of letting it pass through you without demanding a response. You've already survived every impossible day so far, and that stubbornness is proof you're not done writing your own rules yet.",
